// Cyrus plans and pricing copy (r50). PURE, client-safe. The landing's voice: short, concrete, no hype.
// RULES: no prices, no token amounts, no invented stats or testimonials. Everything the owner still has to decide is a
// PLACEHOLDER (see PLACEHOLDERS): the page renders it as a visible, dashed "to be announced" slot so nobody mistakes it
// for a real figure. When the owner decides, pass real values through `PlanValues` (from settings) and nothing else
// changes. Token rules are the product rules from the separation/token work (rollover while subscribed, free tokens
// with servers and renewals); their exact amounts are configurable and never appear in copy.
import type { CyrusModelId } from "../models";

export type PlanId = "free" | CyrusModelId;
export type PlanCopy = {
  id: PlanId; name: string; tier: string; lead: string;
  /** What is included. */
  has: readonly string[];
  /** What is not (shown dimmed). */
  not: readonly string[];
  cta: string;
};

export const PLANS_HEADLINE = { h: "Three tiers.", em: "Pick your power.", sub: "Cyrus builds Minecraft mods today. Every plan installs to your Nxeon servers or downloads as a jar." } as const;

export const PLANS: readonly PlanCopy[] = [
  { id: "katara", name: "Katara", tier: "Tier I", lead: "Code mods from a prompt.",
    has: ["Plan, code, compile, install", "Config sliders", "Install to your Nxeon servers", "Unused tokens roll over while subscribed"],
    not: ["Studios not included"], cta: "Start with Katara" },
  { id: "saka", name: "Saka", tier: "Tier II", lead: "Everything in Katara, with sound.",
    has: ["Everything in Katara", "Sound Studio", "Unused tokens roll over while subscribed"],
    not: ["Texture and 3D studios in Yakko"], cta: "Start with Saka" },
  { id: "yakko", name: "Yakko", tier: "Tier III", lead: "Every model, every studio.",
    has: ["All models", "Texture, Sound and 3D Model studios", "Asset libraries", "Unused tokens roll over while subscribed"],
    not: [], cta: "Start with Yakko" },
8:## Help center, plans page and product copy (r50)
10:- **Help center**: 27 markdown articles in `content/cyrus/help/*.md` (front matter: title, category, order, summary, tags, optional `status: pending`), parsed by a small safe renderer (`lib/cyrus/help/markdown.ts`, a typed tree and React elements, never raw HTML; unsafe link targets become text) and searched by `lib/cyrus/help/search.ts` (every word must match; title > tags > summary > body). Routes: route group `app/(cyrus-help)/cyrus-help` (`/cyrus-help`, `/cyrus-help/<slug>`, `/cyrus-help/plans`), which cyrus.my serves as `/help`, `/help/<slug>` and `/plans` (rewrite in `lib/cyrus/bridge/routing.ts`, reads only). Cross-links use a `help:` target followed by the article slug; a test fails on a dead link, a model family name, a price, a token amount or an emoji. The Mod Packs and modules article is marked **pending** until r45 merges.
